# Frontend
#
# `*.png` above exists for sweep plots, but it matches every frontend image too --
# a favicon or a logo would be dropped silently and only show up as a broken build on a
# fresh clone. These negations undo that for the two directories images live in; they
# work because only a file pattern was excluded above, never a parent directory.
!frontend/public/**/*.png
!frontend/src/assets/**/*.png

# README figures and their evidence are committed, not run output: docs/evidence/ holds
# the untouched result of one real `qecgen sweep` run, docs/make_sweep_plot.py re-plots
# it, and the UI captures are real screenshots. The `*.png`, `*.threshold.json` and
# `*.csv` patterns above exist for run-time outputs and would silently drop these on the
# next `git add`; all three negations work because only file patterns were excluded,
# never a parent directory.
#
# `*.csv` is the newest and the least obvious: it is there because `.csv` is now a
# dataset extension, but it also matches the sweep *results* table, which is a different
# artifact and is committed. Dropping docs/evidence/sweep.csv would break the README
# threshold figure with no error anywhere.
!docs/images/*.png
!docs/evidence/*.threshold.json
!docs/evidence/*.csv

frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/

# Browser-automation scratch output from visual checks.
.playwright-mcp/

# The built bundle. Committing minified JS would put unreviewable diffs in the history of
# a repository whose whole convention is explained changes, so it is built on demand:
# `qecgen ui` names the command when it is missing.
#
# The whole directory, with no `.gitkeep` exception: Vite builds with `emptyOutDir`, which
# wipes anything placed here to hold the directory open. A fresh clone therefore has no
# `static/` at all, which `create_app` handles -- it serves the build instructions and
# leaves the API running.
qecgen/ui/static/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
